  "vertical_datum": "Provider camera height above roadway in metres. The garden paving and the two photographic station ground levels have not been levelled together.",
  "observations": "A, B, C follow the street-facing elevation from east to west. A is the paired glazed casement. B is the adjacent paired shutter. C is the narrower shutter. A separate high pair of small casements occupies the raised attic over A, immediately east of the lower parapet/dormer break. The underlying street wall hides the ground storey.",
  "identity_ties_to_photo_190": [
    "paired higher glazed casements set in the opening next to the east garden corner",
    "lower double shutter B and separate narrow shutter C toward the west with their diminutive openings above",
    "cream lintels, exposed dark aggregate and full-height contrasting downpipe at the B transition"
  ],
  "photo_190_garden_face": "adjacent east-northeast gable facing approximately 67°; street wall faces north-northwest about 335–339°",
  "ray_computation": "For each marked pixel x,y subtract the projected image centre and divide by f=(width/2)/tan(hfov/2). Rotate the optical direction by pitch and true-north azimuth. Compute the 3-D point minimizing the sum of squared distances to the individual 3-D lines. Chainage is horizontal distance along A-to-C.",
