  },
  "attic_candidates": {
    "lower_upper_band": "B and C have top casements directly above their main axes; from roadway datum B approximately 6.6–7.5m and C approximately 6.4–7.0m. Opening limits away from branches carry greater weight.",
    "first_bay": "Eastern street-facing raised light-painted bay has at least two individually framed small openings, and an east-facing glazed triangular gable. The more legible eastern casement in its north wall has its sill about 7.8m and top about 9.0m above the road. The two ends of the western casement are partly hidden.",
    "roof_height": "Northwestern eave tip about 7.8m above road. Local peak and roof-to-wall intersections are on different planes and the overall roof outline is constrained independently in plan.",
    "alternative_common_plane_height": "With the upper individual A opening treated as coplanar with the principal glazed window, 2015 west station gives 60/66 and middle station approximately 86/87 times the 1.40m main opening: about 1.27–1.39m from its head to the attic sill. The unconstrained 3-D estimate is 1.95m; an attic setback changes the relation, and the affected rays pass a tree. The coplanar ratio is preferred for a shared wall plane."
